 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nREGEXP_SUBSTR function generates incorrect SQL with undefined variables\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen transpiling REGEXP_SUBSTR expressions to Snowflake dialect, the function generates SQL with undefined variables, causing syntax errors.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\n\n# This should work but generates invalid SQL\nsql = \"REGEXP_SUBSTR(subject, pattern, pos, occ, params, group)\"\nresult = sqlglot.transpile(sql, write=\"snowflake\")[0]\nprint(result)\n```\n\nThe above code produces SQL with undefined variable references instead of the expected valid Snowflake REGEXP_SUBSTR syntax.\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nThe transpilation should generate valid Snowflake SQL like:\n```sql\nREGEXP_SUBSTR(subject, pattern, pos, occ, params, group)\n```\n\n#### Actual Behavior\n\nThe function generates SQL with undefined variables, making the output invalid and unusable.\n</issue>\n",
